  "tagline": "Agentic coding in the terminal, desktop and cloud.",
  "description": "Claude Code is Anthropic's coding agent. The same agent loop runs in the terminal, IDE extensions, the desktop app, the web and Slack, on your machine, in an Anthropic-managed cloud VM or on self-hosted runners in your organization's network (public beta), and the Claude mobile app connects to those sessions. Model traffic can go straight to Anthropic or a cloud provider, or through a self-hosted gateway, and prompts can be dictated by voice, with transcription on Anthropic's servers. It reads CLAUDE.md or AGENTS.md, keeps auto memory in a MEMORY.md index, searches files with grep and find, delegates to subagents, and is extended with skills, plugins, hooks and MCP. Permission modes range from manual approval to auto mode, where a classifier reviews actions, and telemetry can be exported over OpenTelemetry. The same loop is available as a library, the Claude Agent SDK. The source code is closed, but Anthropic documents the architecture in depth.",
